<div style="border: 2px solid #1a5276; padding: 15px; text-align: center; background-color: #e0f2f7;">
    <h1 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 5</h1>
    <p style="color: #1a5276; margin: 5px 0 0 0;"><em>Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</em></p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 5</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Mediation</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 12th Grade (CEFR: B1.3)</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> My Personal Success Story</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> Saving for Future Goals!</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Mediation: Text: Summarize technical instructions clearly. Communication: Facilitate diverse group discussions.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Mediation: Can summarize technical instructions on budgeting and lead group activities to practice these steps (e.g., "Let's create a group budget for a school trip. First, we list our expenses. Then, we compare costs and agree on how much each team member will contribute.")</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Can facilitate group discussions on personal goals using supportive body language to encourage engagement (e.g., nods and gestures to encourage classmates to share their future goals).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Can clarify technical terms in English and Spanish for diverse groups (e.g., "Budgeting means planning your money, like how you decide to save five dollars every month for your future goals.").</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 30%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 50%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 20%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher starts by displaying an infographic titled "5 Smart Steps to Save for Your Future Goals." Students work in pairs to quickly discuss the main idea of each step, practicing summarizing. The teacher asks, "What is the most important message from step 3?" (related to "savings" and "investment").</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models how to clarify a technical term. "For example, 'investment' means putting your money into something like stocks or property with the hope of making more money in the future. It's like planting a seed to grow a big tree, but with your finances. Have you ever considered an 'investment'?" The teacher explicitly demonstrates stressing content words ("INVESTMENT," "MONEY," "FUTURE") and reducing stress on auxiliary verbs.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b> The teacher checks understanding of the concept of "clarifying technical terms" and "summarizing."</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">CCQ 1: "If I ask you to 'summarize' this article, do I want every detail or just the main points?" (Expected: Main points).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">CCQ 2: "When I 'clarify' a technical term like 'budgeting,' am I making it more complicated or easier to understand?" (Expected: Easier to understand).</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "My Personal Success Story")</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> Students are presented with a short, technical guide titled "Your Success Story Blog: Technical Setup and Budgeting Tips for Your Future Goals," outlining steps for creating an online blog, including sections on "Content Structure," "SEO Optimization," and "Financial Planning for Blog Growth." This content introduces terms like "SEO" (Search Engine Optimization) and reinforces "financial planning" and "budgeting."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Students will understand technical instructions related to an online project and identify key terms that require clarification for a general audience. They will also recognize instances where Present Perfect, Future Continuous, and First Conditional are used within the text to discuss past achievements, future goals, and potential opportunities for their blog.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Gist Question: "What is the primary purpose of this guide?" (Expected: To help students set up and plan the financial aspect of their 'Success Story Blog').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">True/False: Students read statements based on the text, e.g., "SEO Optimization is about making your blog look pretty." (False).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Identify Technical Terms: Students highlight three terms from the guide that they believe a classmate might need help understanding (e.g., "SEO," "monetization," "revenue streams").</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Accuracy focus on Mediation)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Practice summarizing instructions, clarifying technical vocabulary ("finances," "investment," "strategies," "growth," "achievements"), and using grammatical structures (Present perfect, Future continuous, First conditional) for personal success stories. Focus on stressing content words (nouns, main verbs, adjectives) and reducing auxiliary stress.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: decimal; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Controlled Practice: Summarizing Budgeting Steps.</b> The teacher provides sentences with technical budgeting instructions from the "Financial Planning for Blog Growth" section. Students rewrite these sentences in simpler terms. E.g., Original: "Allocate a portion of your monthly revenue for content creation and marketing initiatives." Student summary: "You need to save some money each month for writing and promoting your blog." They practice saying, "I have saved some money for my blog," stressing "SAVED" and "MONEY."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Semi-controlled Practice: Clarifying Technical Terms.</b> In pairs, students receive cards with technical terms (e.g., "SEO," "monetization," "investment," "network"). Student A picks a card and explains the term to Student B in simple English. Student B can ask for clarification or a Spanish equivalent if needed, promoting the "clarify technical terms in English and Spanish for diverse groups" learning outcome. E.g., "SEO means making your website easier for search engines to find, like Google. In Spanish, we could say 'optimización para motores de búsqueda.'" They practice using phrases like, "If you improve your SEO, you will find more opportunities." stressing "IMPROVE" and "OPPORTUNITIES."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pair Interaction/Peer Check: Explaining Blog Project Steps.</b> Students work in new pairs. One student explains a specific section of the "Success Story Blog" project instructions (e.g., "How to plan your content," "How to manage your finances for the blog") to their partner, summarizing key points and clarifying any potential jargon. The partner listens for clarity and provides feedback on whether they understood the summary and clarifications. They use future continuous to talk about their blog: "In six months, I will be managing the content calendar." stressing "SIX MONTHS," "MANAGING," and "CONTENT CALENDAR."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "My Personal Success Story")</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Group Discussion Facilitation and Project Explanation.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b> Students form small groups (3-4 members). Each student takes turns acting as a facilitator, explaining one core aspect of their "Success Story Blog" project (e.g., their personal "growth" narrative, their "financial strategies" for blog "sustainability," or their "community service" impact related to the blog). The facilitator must:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Briefly summarize the chosen aspect of their blog project using the target grammar (Present perfect for achievements, Future continuous for long-term goals, First conditional for future success). E.g., "I have successfully completed the initial planning for my blog. In the next few months, I will be developing content. If I continue to work diligently, I will achieve a wide audience."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarify any technical terms from the "Your Success Story Blog: Technical Setup and Budgeting Tips" guide that might apply to their section (e.g., "monetization," "engagement," "sustainable finances") for their group, offering Spanish equivalents if appropriate for clarity.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Facilitate a short group discussion (2-3 minutes) by asking questions like, "What financial strategies do you think are most important for a new blog?" or "How do you plan to build your online network?" The facilitator must use supportive body language (nods, open gestures) to encourage participation and ensure all voices are heard and respected.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students should actively practice stressing content words in their explanations and reducing stress on auxiliary verbs for natural speech.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Role:</b> Circulates, observes, provides support for clarification, and notes effective facilitation and language use.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Formative assessment strategy)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher Observation Checklist and Peer Assessment (Focus on Mediation Skills).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Each student's facilitation during the group discussion in Stage 4 is assessed. Peers use a simple checklist to evaluate the facilitator's ability to summarize, clarify, and lead the discussion effectively.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher Checklist/Peer Feedback Form):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity of summarization of blog project aspects.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Accuracy and clarity in clarifying technical terms (English and/or Spanish).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Effective use of target vocabulary (e.g., "finances," "strategies," "growth," "achievements," "opportunities").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate use of Present perfect, Future continuous, and First conditional.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Supportive body language and techniques to encourage group engagement.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Intelligible pronunciation with appropriate stress on content words.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete a short reflection.</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was one technical term you successfully clarified for your group today, and how did you do it?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How did you encourage your classmates to share their ideas, and what body language did you use?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Concluding the lesson and looking ahead)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Reflecting on today's lesson, how has practicing mediation skills improved your ability to discuss your future goals and financial strategies more clearly with others?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What specific skill in mediating discussions or explaining complex ideas do you feel you still need to improve for your future career?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What aspects of explaining the "Success Story Blog" project and clarifying terms went well? Did students effectively use supportive body language and stress content words for clarity?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What challenges did students face in summarizing or facilitating discussions? What adjustments or scaffolds (e.g., more sentence starters for clarification, clearer rubrics for facilitation) are needed for future mediation tasks?</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson in the theme sequence:</b> This lesson concludes the theme "Saving for Future Goals!" and the "Success Story Blog" project. The next sequence will begin a new theme, likely building on students' skills in planning and communication, perhaps involving presenting these completed blog projects in a more formal setting or applying mediation skills to community-based projects.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>